From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:05:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(food):=20honest=20energy=20balance=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20no=20double-counted=20resting=20energy,=20the=20str?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ap=20counts,=20day=20close?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The strap's day figure (active_kcal = DailyMetric.activeKcalEst) is
  resting + activity; FoodEnergy added a basal on top of it whenever the
  phone had no active energy, inventing ~1,700 kcal of deficit. Every
  candidate is now a total (strap, phone active + resting, resting only)
  and the highest wins: each source only misses energy (strap off the
  wrist, phone blind to gym work), so the largest is the most complete.
- Today shows where the day closes if nothing more is eaten (so far + the
  rest of the day at rest: scale BMR, else the profile's Harris–Benedict,
  the formula the strap estimate uses).
- Past days in the Food tab show their burn and balance; the coach gets the
  previous 7 days' balance and where today closes.
- Upstream's AdaptiveExpenditureEngine (intake + weight trend), unused until
  now, feeds a "Your real burn" card and a coach line, next to the app's
  own average estimate over the same days; until it has 3 weeks it says
  how many meal days and weigh-ins it still needs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
